# Accepted findings. Every entry needs: ID, reason, owner, expiry date.
# Entries are reviewed in PRs like code; expired entries are removed.
# Format:  <ID>  then a comment line with reason — owner — expiry.

# Terraform state storage account allows public network access (default action Allow).
# Reason: GitHub-hosted runners have no fixed egress IPs, so an IP allow-list would
# break CI; private endpoint + self-hosted runner has a cost ($0 budget).
# Mitigation: shared keys disabled (Entra ID auth only), TLS 1.2, no public blobs,
# RBAC scoped to the tfstate container, versioning + soft delete.
# Owner: platform — expires 2026-12-31
AZU-0012
